Day 3: Setting Up Switch-to-Switch Trunking & Fixing Interface Drops


Day 2 Context: Created VLANs 10 through 60 and configured user access ports across both switches.

---

What I Built
1. Configured Trunking on Both Switches:
   Selected the inter-switch link (`GigabitEthernet0/1`) on SW1 and SW2 and configured it to carry traffic across all six VLANs:
   ```hs
   enable
   configure terminal
   interface GigabitEthernet0/1
    switchport mode trunk
    switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,40,50,60
   end

2.	Verified Layer 2 Connectivity: Ran show interfaces trunk to make sure the link was actively trunking using 802.1q. Checked show mac address-table to confirm that MAC addresses from devices on SW2 were showing up on SW1 across the trunk.
3.	Break/Fix Scenario (Simulating a Config Error):
o	The Break: Accidentally removed VLANs 50 and 60 on SW2 using switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,40.
o	The Impact: Devices on those pruned VLANs instantly lost the ability to communicate across the switch link.
o	The Fix: Restored the allowed list with switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,40,50,60 and verified that traffic was restored.
Real-World Troubleshooting: Resolving the Gi0/1 Down/Down Link
While setting up the topology, GigabitEthernet0/1 refused to come up and stayed stuck in a down, line protocol is down (disabled) state. Here is how I tracked down the root cause and fixed it:
•	Checking Admin Status: I ran no shutdown on Gi0/1 on both switches first, but the interface stayed disabled.
•	Catching CLI Syntax Shortcuts: Realized that typing brief shortcuts like in g0/1 was accidentally targeting a system interface template (Lance hardware) rather than the physical Gigabit port.
•	Fixing the Physical Layer: The interface output flagged a speed/duplex mismatch (100Mb/s Half-duplex). In Packet Tracer, using the wrong cable type locks the interface. I swapped out the connection for a Copper Crossover cable directly between Gi0/1 on both switches and explicitly ran no shutdown on gigabitEthernet 0/1. The link instantly came up!
